---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactCta from '../components/ContactCta.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
import { experience } from '../data/experience';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Engineer turned product leader: Gautam Khanna's path from building payment systems in Singapore to leading real-time payments products at Visa in London."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Engineer turned product leader</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I spent more than a decade as a software engineer, much of it on payment systems, before I started deciding
        what those systems should do next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        I am a Director of Product Management at Visa, where I lead money movement and real-time payments products
        within Visa Direct. The work is building API-driven payment platforms that let banks, fintechs and enterprise
        clients move funds securely and compliantly, across regions and use cases.
      </p>
      <p>
        I came to product through engineering. I started in 2010 as an application developer on the Vocalink payment
        infrastructure project, then spent nine years in Singapore as a software engineer at Cognizant, NCS Group and
        Visa. I moved to London with Visa in 2021 and from engineering into product management in 2022.
      </p>
      <p>
        That background shapes how I work. I can go deep with engineering, risk, compliance and operations teams, and
        still keep the client's experience in view: how they onboard, how they integrate, and how quickly they get to
        value. Years of working on mission-critical systems also left me with a bias for resilience, scale and
        transaction integrity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside the core portfolio I drive applied AI work: capabilities that improve decisions, automation and
        client experience in payments, and tools that help product teams get to insight and prioritise faster. In a
        regulated business, that means balancing new ideas against risk, compliance and trust.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <ol class="timeline">
        {
          experience.map((employer) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{employer.company}</h3>
              <ul class="roles">
                {employer.roles.map((role) => (
                  <li>
                    <span>{role.title}</span>
                    <span class="role-meta">
                      {role.location ? `${role.period}, ${role.location}` : role.period}
                    </span>
                    {role.summary && <p class="role-summary">{role.summary}</p>}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Education and certifications</h2>
      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>
          {profile.education.degree}
          <span class="item-meta">{profile.education.school}, {profile.education.years}</span>
        </li>
        {
          profile.certifications.map((cert) => (
            <li>
              {cert.name}
              <span class="item-meta">
                {cert.issuer}, {cert.year}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="muted languages">Languages: {profile.languages.join(', ')}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <ContactCta />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .languages {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
